{"id":"rf01","title":"Photosynthesis","text":"Photosynthesis is the process by which plants {1} light energy into chemical energy. Chlorophyll, the green pigment found in chloroplasts, {2} sunlight, mainly in the red and blue wavelengths. The absorbed energy is used to {3} carbon dioxide and water into glucose, while oxygen is released as a by-product. Without this process, most life on Earth would not {4}, since it forms the base of nearly every food chain. Scientists continue to study how the reaction could be {5} artificially in order to produce clean fuel.","blanks":[{"options":["weigh","divide","convert","borrow"],"answer":2},{"options":["rejects","hides","absorbs","stores"],"answer":2},{"options":["transform","remove","delay","measure"],"answer":0},{"options":["survived","survival","surviving","survive"],"answer":3},{"options":["replicating","replicated","replicate","replication"],"answer":1}],"tip":"Look at the word before the gap: 'would not' needs a base verb, and 'could be' needs a past participle.","tipAr":"بعد 'would not' لازم فعل في المصدر (survive)، وبعد 'could be' لازم التصريف الثالث (replicated). وكلمة absorbs تتماشى مع chlorophyll وsunlight."},
{"id":"rf02","title":"The Industrial Revolution","text":"The Industrial Revolution began in Britain in the late eighteenth century and gradually {1} to other parts of Europe and North America. The invention of the steam engine allowed factories to be built far from rivers, which had previously {2} the main source of power. As a result, millions of people moved from rural areas to cities in search of work, and urban populations grew {3}. Living conditions were often poor, and it was not until the nineteenth century that governments introduced laws to {4} workers from dangerous conditions. The changes of this period still {5} the way modern economies operate.","blanks":[{"options":["spread","spreading","was spread","spreads"],"answer":0},{"options":["been","being","be","is"],"answer":0},{"options":["more rapid","rapid","rapidly","rapidity"],"answer":2},{"options":["expose","blame","protect","ignore"],"answer":2},{"options":["shaped","shape","shapes","shaping"],"answer":1}],"tip":"Past perfect 'had previously' is followed by 'been'. 'Grew' is a verb, so it takes an adverb.","tipAr":"'had previously' يتبعها been. و'grew' فعل فيحتاج ظرف (rapidly). وcollocation: protect workers from."},
{"id":"rf03","title":"Machine Learning","text":"Machine learning is a branch of computer science in which systems improve their performance by {1} patterns in large amounts of data rather than following fixed instructions. For example, an email filter can learn to {2} spam after being shown thousands of labelled messages. The quality of the results depends heavily {3} the data used for training; if the data is biased, the system will {4} reproduce that bias. For this reason, researchers argue that developers should be held {5} for the decisions their programs make.","blanks":[{"options":["identifies","identify","identified","identifying"],"answer":3},{"options":["recognised","recognise","recognising","recognition"],"answer":1},{"options":["at","by","in","on"],"answer":3},{"options":["never","hardly","rarely","simply"],"answer":3},{"options":["accounting","accounted","account","accountable"],"answer":3}],"tip":"A preposition is followed by an -ing form ('by identifying'). Fixed phrases: depend on, held accountable.","tipAr":"بعد حرف الجر by نستخدم -ing. وعبارات ثابتة: depend on و held accountable."},
{"id":"rf04","title":"Inflation","text":"Inflation refers to a sustained rise in the general level of prices, which {1} the purchasing power of money over time. Central banks usually try to keep inflation at a low and stable level, often around two per cent a year. When prices rise too quickly, they can {2} interest rates to make borrowing more expensive and so slow down spending. However, this policy has {3} effects, since higher rates may also discourage businesses from investing. Economists therefore {4} that there is no simple solution, and that policymakers must balance several goals {5} once.","blanks":[{"options":["protects","doubles","raises","reduces"],"answer":3},{"options":["ignore","raise","freeze","lower"],"answer":1},{"options":["rear","side","back","edge"],"answer":1},{"options":["argue","describe","debate","discuss"],"answer":0},{"options":["in","on","at","by"],"answer":2}],"tip":"Use the logic of the sentence: higher rates make borrowing more expensive, so banks 'raise' them. 'Argue that' is followed by a clause; 'discuss' and 'debate' are not.","tipAr":"المنطق: لو رفعوا الفائدة يصير الاقتراض أغلى (raise). وكلمة argue هي الوحيدة اللي تجي بعدها that. وعبارات ثابتة: side effects و at once."},
{"id":"rf05","title":"Language Change","text":"All living languages change over time. New words are {1} to describe new inventions, while older words fall out of use or acquire different meanings. The English word nice, for instance, once meant foolish before it {2} its modern sense in the eighteenth century. Linguists describe these changes without judging them as good or bad, {3} they regard language as a system that adapts to the needs of its speakers. Attempts to prevent change, such as official academies, have generally had {4} success. Most scholars therefore accept that change is {5} and cannot be stopped.","blanks":[{"options":["coins","coined","coin","coining"],"answer":1},{"options":["acquire","acquired","acquiring","acquires"],"answer":1},{"options":["because","until","although","unless"],"answer":0},{"options":["limited","limiting","limits","limit"],"answer":0},{"options":["inevitably","inevitable","inevitableness","inevitability"],"answer":1}],"tip":"Passive voice needs a past participle ('are coined'). After 'is', use an adjective.","tipAr":"المبني للمجهول يحتاج التصريف الثالث (are coined). وبعد is نستخدم صفة (inevitable). وعبارة because للتعليل."},
{"id":"rf06","title":"The Reliability of Memory","text":"Human memory is not a perfect recording of past events. The psychologist Elizabeth Loftus showed that the wording of a question can {1} what people remember about an accident: witnesses who heard the word smashed estimated higher speeds than those who heard hit. Such findings suggest that memories are {2} reconstructed each time they are recalled, rather than simply retrieved. This has important {3} for the legal system, where eyewitness testimony is often treated as {4} evidence. Courts are therefore {5} cautious about relying on it alone.","blanks":[{"options":["alternate","altering","alter","altered"],"answer":2},{"options":["barely","rarely","hardly","actively"],"answer":3},{"options":["imitations","implementations","indications","implications"],"answer":3},{"options":["reliance","reliable","reliably","relying"],"answer":1},{"options":["increasing","increasingly","increased","increase"],"answer":1}],"tip":"'Can' is followed by a base verb. 'Implications for' is a common academic collocation. Before a noun use an adjective, before an adjective use an adverb.","tipAr":"بعد can فعل مصدر (alter). وcollocation: important implications for. وقبل الاسم evidence نستخدم صفة reliable."},
{"id":"rf07","title":"Coral Reefs","text":"Coral reefs cover less than one per cent of the ocean floor, yet they {1} about a quarter of all marine species. Corals live in partnership with tiny algae that provide them with food through photosynthesis. When the water becomes too warm, the corals expel the algae, {2} them to turn white, a process known as bleaching. If temperatures return to normal quickly, the corals can {3}, but prolonged heat often kills them. Scientists warn that, unless greenhouse gas emissions are {4} significantly, many reefs may disappear {5} the end of the century.","blanks":[{"options":["support","suppress","suppose","supplant"],"answer":0},{"options":["caused","causing","cause","causes"],"answer":1},{"options":["recede","recover","relieve","reject"],"answer":1},{"options":["reducing","reduce","reduction","reduced"],"answer":3},{"options":["until","during","by","since"],"answer":2}],"tip":"Words that look alike (support/suppress/suppose) are common distractors, so check the meaning. 'By the end of' means before or at that time.","tipAr":"انتبه للكلمات المتشابهة في الشكل (support/suppress). وبعد unless ... are نحتاج اسم مفعول (reduced). وby the end of يعني قبل نهاية القرن."},
{"id":"rf08","title":"Roman Concrete","text":"Roman engineers developed a type of concrete that has {1} for two thousand years in some structures, such as the Pantheon in Rome, whose dome remains the largest unreinforced concrete dome in the world. The mixture combined lime with volcanic ash, which reacted chemically to form a durable material that could even {2} underwater. Recent research suggests that small white lumps of lime in the concrete allowed cracks to {3} themselves when water entered. Modern builders are keen to copy this property, as repairing damaged concrete is {4} expensive and the production of cement {5} large amounts of carbon dioxide.","blanks":[{"options":["survives","survived","surviving","survive"],"answer":1},{"options":["sat","set","seat","sit"],"answer":1},{"options":["repairing","repaired","repair","repairs"],"answer":2},{"options":["extremity","extremes","extremely","extreme"],"answer":2},{"options":["release","releasing","released","releases"],"answer":3}],"tip":"'Has' + past participle makes the present perfect. The subject 'production' is singular, so the verb takes -s.","tipAr":"has + التصريف الثالث (survived). وbefore صفة نستخدم ظرف (extremely expensive). والفاعل production مفرد فالفعل releases."},
{"id":"rf09","title":"How Vaccines Work","text":"A vaccine trains the immune system to recognise a disease-causing organism without {1} the person ill. It usually contains a weakened or inactive form of the germ, or a harmless piece of it. When the body meets this substance, it produces antibodies and also creates memory cells that can {2} the real infection much faster in the future. Smallpox, a disease that killed millions of people, was {3} eradicated in 1980 thanks to a worldwide vaccination campaign. Today, many experts believe that polio could be the next disease to be {4} eliminated, although progress has been {5} by conflict and misinformation.","blanks":[{"options":["make","making","makes","made"],"answer":1},{"options":["spread","cause","fight","ignore"],"answer":2},{"options":["officially","official","officialdom","officiate"],"answer":0},{"options":["completed","complete","completing","completely"],"answer":3},{"options":["slows","slow","slowed","slowing"],"answer":2}],"tip":"After a preposition ('without') use -ing. An adverb can sit between 'be' and a participle ('be completely eliminated').","tipAr":"بعد without نستخدم -ing (making). والظرف يجي بين be والتصريف الثالث (be completely eliminated). ومعنى fight: تحارب العدوى."},
{"id":"rf10","title":"Supply and Demand","text":"In a market economy, the price of a product is largely {1} by supply and demand. When demand for a good rises while supply remains the same, sellers can {2} higher prices. If, on the other hand, supply increases faster than demand, prices tend to fall. This simple model helps to explain why fruit is cheaper during the harvest season than in winter. However, real markets are more complicated, because consumers do not always {3} rationally and governments sometimes intervene by setting maximum prices. Economists therefore use the model as a starting point {4} than as a complete description of {5} markets behave.","blanks":[{"options":["determined","determines","determining","determine"],"answer":0},{"options":["change","charge","choose","carry"],"answer":1},{"options":["behaving","behaved","behave","behaviour"],"answer":2},{"options":["other","better","rather","instead"],"answer":2},{"options":["what","why","how","which"],"answer":2}],"tip":"Passive voice: 'is largely determined by'. The fixed pattern is 'a starting point rather than ...'.","tipAr":"مبني للمجهول: is determined by. وبعد do not always نحتاج مصدر (behave). والتركيب الثابت: rather than. و'how markets behave' بمعنى كيف تتصرف الأسواق."},
{"id":"rf11","title":"Black Holes","text":"A black hole is a region of space where gravity is so strong that nothing, not even light, can {1} from it. Most black holes form when a massive star runs out of fuel and its core collapses under its own weight. The boundary beyond which escape is impossible is known as the event horizon. Because black holes emit no light, astronomers cannot observe them {2}; instead, they detect them by studying the effect on nearby stars and gas. In 2019, the Event Horizon Telescope produced the first image of a black hole's shadow, {3} in the galaxy Messier 87. This achievement required {4} between telescopes on several continents, whose data were combined by powerful computers.","blanks":[{"options":["arrive","escape","enter","approach"],"answer":1},{"options":["directness","directly","directed","direct"],"answer":1},{"options":["location","located","locating","locates"],"answer":1},{"options":["cooperating","cooperation","cooperate","cooperative"],"answer":1}],"tip":"Four blanks here. 'Escape from' fits the physics; an adverb modifies the verb 'observe'; 'located in' is a reduced passive; after 'required' use a noun.","tipAr":"escape from منطقية فيزيائياً. والظرف directly يعدّل الفعل observe. وlocated in = موجود في. وبعد required نحتاج اسم (cooperation)."},
{"id":"rf12","title":"Gothic Architecture","text":"Gothic architecture emerged in France in the twelfth century and is {1} by pointed arches, ribbed vaults and large stained-glass windows. Earlier Romanesque churches had thick walls and small windows because the walls had to {2} the weight of the roof. Gothic builders solved this problem with flying buttresses, external stone supports that {3} the outward pressure of the vaults to the ground. This innovation made it possible to build much taller buildings filled with light. Cathedrals such as Notre-Dame in Paris were symbols of civic pride, and their construction often {4} several generations, with some projects {5} unfinished for centuries.","blanks":[{"options":["characterise","characterising","characterised","characteristic"],"answer":2},{"options":["supply","suppress","suppose","support"],"answer":3},{"options":["transferred","transferring","transfer","transfers"],"answer":2},{"options":["span","spanned","spans","spanning"],"answer":1},{"options":["leaves","leaving","left","leave"],"answer":2}],"tip":"'Is characterised by' is a fixed passive. 'Supports' is plural, so the verb has no -s. 'Left unfinished' is a past participle.","tipAr":"is characterised by تركيب ثابت. والفاعل supports جمع فالفعل بدون s (transfer). وleft unfinished = بقيت غير مكتملة."},
{"id":"rf13","title":"Why We Sleep","text":"Adults need between seven and nine hours of sleep a night, yet surveys suggest that a large proportion of people regularly get {1}. During sleep, the brain moves through cycles of light sleep, deep sleep and rapid eye movement sleep. Deep sleep appears to be important for physical repair, {2} REM sleep is linked to memory and emotional processing. Researchers have found that students who sleep well after studying {3} better on tests than those who stay up all night. Chronic sleep deprivation has also been associated with a higher {4} of heart disease and obesity. Doctors therefore {5} that people keep regular bedtimes and avoid screens before sleeping.","blanks":[{"options":["less","little","least","lower"],"answer":0},{"options":["therefore","unless","because","whereas"],"answer":3},{"options":["perform","performed","performing","performs"],"answer":0},{"options":["risk","wish","choice","hope"],"answer":0},{"options":["suggests","wants","recommend","tells"],"answer":2}],"tip":"'Whereas' contrasts two things. 'Risk of' is the usual collocation with disease. The subject 'students' is plural, so use 'perform'.","tipAr":"whereas للمقارنة بين شيئين. وrisk of heart disease collocation. والفاعل students جمع فالفعل perform بدون s."},
{"id":"rf14","title":"Urbanisation","text":"In 2007, for the first time in history, more than half of the world's population lived in cities. The United Nations projects that this proportion will reach nearly seventy per cent by 2050. Cities offer jobs, education and healthcare, {1} explains why so many people move to them. However, rapid growth can place enormous pressure on housing and transport, and in many developing countries a large number of residents live in informal settlements {2} access to clean water. Urban planners argue that well-designed public transport and higher-density housing can {3} congestion and pollution. They also stress that cities must {4} to climate change, for example by protecting low-lying districts from {5}.","blanks":[{"options":["what","who","that","which"],"answer":3},{"options":["without","with","within","through"],"answer":0},{"options":["increase","reduce","introduce","produce"],"answer":1},{"options":["adapt","adopt","adjoin","adept"],"answer":0},{"options":["flooding","have flooded","flood","flooded"],"answer":0}],"tip":"'Which' can refer to a whole previous clause. 'Adapt to' is the right collocation, not 'adopt to'.","tipAr":"which تشير إلى الجملة السابقة كاملة. وadapt to = يتكيف مع (وليس adopt). وبعد حرف الجر from نستخدم اسم أو -ing."},
{"id":"rf15","title":"Renewable Energy","text":"Solar and wind power are now among the cheapest sources of new electricity in many countries, a dramatic change from two decades ago. One challenge remains: the sun does not always shine and the wind does not always blow, so supply can {1} from hour to hour. Batteries and pumped-water storage can {2} surplus energy for use later, but they add to the overall cost. Some countries are therefore investing in a wider electricity grid, which would allow regions with excess power to send it to areas {3} demand is high. Experts say that a combination of technologies, rather than a single solution, is {4} to meet future needs.","blanks":[{"options":["fluctuated","fluctuation","fluctuating","fluctuate"],"answer":3},{"options":["explore","store","ignore","restore"],"answer":1},{"options":["which","where","who","what"],"answer":1},{"options":["necessary","necessarily","necessity","necessitate"],"answer":0}],"tip":"After modal 'can' use the base verb. 'Where' follows a place noun ('areas where'). After 'is' use an adjective.","tipAr":"'areas where' لأن areas مكان. وبعد can فعل مصدر. وبعد is نستخدم صفة (necessary)."},
{"id":"rf16","title":"The Printing Press","text":"Around 1440, Johannes Gutenberg introduced movable metal type to Europe, {1} the production of books far faster and cheaper than copying them by hand. Before this invention, a single book could take months to produce, so most people never owned one. Within fifty years, printing presses were operating in more than two hundred European towns. Ideas now {2} quickly across borders, and literacy rates gradually rose. The Reformation, which began in 1517, benefited greatly from the new technology, as Martin Luther's writings were printed in thousands of copies. Historians still debate how far the press was {3} for the scientific revolution, but few deny that it {4} the spread of knowledge.","blanks":[{"options":["makes","make","making","made"],"answer":2},{"options":["travelled","travels","travelling","travel"],"answer":0},{"options":["response","responsible","responsibly","responding"],"answer":1},{"options":["accelerate","accelerated","accelerates","accelerating"],"answer":1}],"tip":"Participle phrase: 'introduced ..., making ...'. 'Responsible for' is a fixed phrase.","tipAr":"making جملة وصفية بعد الفاصلة. وresponsible for تركيب ثابت."},
{"id":"rf17","title":"Bilingualism","text":"For much of the twentieth century, many educators believed that growing up with two languages confused children and slowed their development. Modern research has {1} this view. Bilingual children may mix languages in a single sentence at first, but this is a normal stage rather than a sign of difficulty. Studies suggest that managing two languages gives the brain regular practice in switching attention, which may improve certain executive skills. Some research has even indicated that bilingualism can {2} the onset of dementia by several years, although scientists remain {3} about how strong the effect is. What is clear is that bilingual people {4} benefit from wider job opportunities and cultural understanding.","blanks":[{"options":["confirmed","repeated","overturned","ignored"],"answer":2},{"options":["deny","deliver","delay","derive"],"answer":2},{"options":["curious","careless","cautious","certain"],"answer":2},{"options":["frequently","frequented","frequency","frequent"],"answer":0}],"tip":"The logic 'Modern research has ___ this view' needs a negative result, because the old view was mistaken. 'Cautious about' fits 'remain'.","tipAr":"المنطق: البحث الحديث 'أبطل' (overturned) الفكرة القديمة الخاطئة. وremain cautious about = لا يزالون حذرين بشأن."},
{"id":"rf18","title":"Plate Tectonics","text":"The Earth's outer shell is divided into several large plates that move slowly over the hot, partly molten layer beneath them. The plates travel at roughly the speed at which fingernails grow, yet over millions of years this movement has {1} the oceans and continents. Most earthquakes and volcanoes occur along plate boundaries, where plates collide, pull apart or slide past one another. The Himalayas, for example, are still rising because the Indian plate is pushing {2} the Eurasian plate. Although scientists cannot yet {3} exactly when an earthquake will strike, they can identify regions of high risk and recommend that buildings {4} to withstand shaking.","blanks":[{"options":["reshaped","reshapes","reshape","reshaping"],"answer":0},{"options":["against","beside","above","from"],"answer":0},{"options":["prefer","predict","prevent","prepare"],"answer":1},{"options":["be designed","designed","designing","being designed"],"answer":0}],"tip":"'Recommend that buildings be designed' uses the subjunctive. 'Predict when' is the natural collocation.","tipAr":"بعد recommend that نستخدم be + التصريف الثالث (be designed). وpredict تعني يتنبأ، وهي المناسبة مع earthquake."},
{"id":"rf19","title":"Antibiotic Resistance","text":"Antibiotics have saved millions of lives since penicillin was first used widely in the 1940s. However, bacteria can evolve, and some strains have become {1} to drugs that once killed them. Every time antibiotics are used, a few bacteria may survive and pass on their resistant genes. Using these medicines when they are not needed, such as for viral infections, {2} the problem. The World Health Organization has warned that, {3} new drugs are developed, common infections could become untreatable. Doctors therefore urge patients to complete their prescribed course {4} to stop treatment early, even when they feel better.","blanks":[{"options":["resistance","resistant","resisting","resist"],"answer":1},{"options":["worsens","worsen","worsening","worsened"],"answer":0},{"options":["because","although","while","unless"],"answer":3},{"options":["in case of","owing to","as well as","rather than"],"answer":3}],"tip":"'Become resistant to' needs an adjective. 'Unless new drugs are developed' = if new drugs are not developed.","tipAr":"become + صفة (resistant). وunless = إذا لم. وrather than = بدلاً من أن."},
{"id":"rf20","title":"Globalisation","text":"Globalisation describes the growing connection of economies, cultures and populations through trade, investment and technology. Since the middle of the twentieth century, falling transport costs and the spread of the internet have {1} companies to manufacture goods in one country and sell them in dozens of others. Supporters argue that this process has lifted millions out of poverty, particularly in East Asia. Critics, {2}, point out that it has also contributed to job losses in some industries and widened the gap between rich and poor within countries. The disruption caused by the 2020 pandemic led many firms to {3} their supply chains, and some governments now {4} greater national self-sufficiency in essential goods.","blanks":[{"options":["enables","enabling","enabled","enable"],"answer":2},{"options":["therefore","however","besides","moreover"],"answer":1},{"options":["reconsidering","reconsidered","reconsiders","reconsider"],"answer":3},{"options":["favour","favoured","favouring","favours"],"answer":0}],"tip":"'Critics, however, point out' contrasts with the supporters in the previous sentence. After 'led many firms to' use the base verb.","tipAr":"however للتناقض مع آراء المؤيدين. وبعد led ... to نستخدم الفعل المصدر. وgovernments (جمع) فالفعل favour بدون s."},
{"id":"rf21","title":"Green Roofs","text":"A green roof is a roof covered with vegetation planted over a waterproof layer. These roofs are becoming {1} in crowded cities, where there is little space for parks. In summer, the plants and soil keep buildings cooler because they {2} heat rather than absorbing it as dark roofing does. They also hold rainwater, which reduces the pressure on drains during heavy storms. In addition, they provide a habitat for insects and birds. The main drawback is that they are heavier and more expensive to install than ordinary roofs, {3} the structure must be strong enough to carry the extra weight. Nevertheless, several cities now {4} developers to include them in new buildings.","blanks":[{"options":["popularly","popularise","popularity","popular"],"answer":3},{"options":["reflex","reflect","reject","respect"],"answer":1},{"options":["until","although","unless","since"],"answer":3},{"options":["required","require","requiring","requires"],"answer":1}],"tip":"'Become' + adjective. A green roof does not 'absorb' heat like dark roofing; it cools by evaporation, and the contrast 'rather than absorbing' signals an opposite verb.","tipAr":"بعد become نستخدم صفة (popular). والمعنى 'تقلل الحرارة بدل امتصاصها'. وsince هنا بمعنى لأن. وcities جمع فالفعل require بدون s."},
{"id":"rf22","title":"The Silk Road","text":"The Silk Road was not a single road but a network of trade routes that linked China with the Mediterranean for more than a thousand years. Merchants rarely travelled the whole distance; instead, goods passed through many hands, {1} their price rose at each stage. Silk was the most famous product, but spices, glass, paper and precious metals were also traded. The routes carried ideas {2} well as goods: Buddhism spread from India into China, and the technology of papermaking moved westward. Sadly, the same routes helped to {3} diseases, and the Black Death is thought to have reached Europe along trade routes in the fourteenth century. The network declined when sea routes became {4} and safer.","blanks":[{"options":["so that","even if","as long as","in case"],"answer":0},{"options":["like","so","than","as"],"answer":3},{"options":["spreads","spread","spreading","spreader"],"answer":1},{"options":["fast","faster","fastest","fastly"],"answer":1}],"tip":"'As well as' is a fixed phrase. Comparison: 'faster and safer' needs two comparatives.","tipAr":"as well as تركيب ثابت. والمقارنة 'faster and safer' تحتاج صيغة مقارنة للصفتين. وبعد help to نستخدم مصدر."},
{"id":"rf23","title":"Gross Domestic Product","text":"Gross domestic product, or GDP, measures the total value of goods and services produced within a country in a given period. Governments and economists use it as an {1} of economic health: when GDP grows, businesses are usually expanding and employment is rising. However, GDP has well-known limitations. It does not {2} unpaid work such as childcare at home, and it makes no distinction between activities that improve well-being and those that harm it. For example, money spent on cleaning up an oil spill {3} to GDP, even though the spill damaged the environment. For these reasons, some researchers propose supplementing it with measures of health, education and happiness {4} reflect quality of life more fully.","blanks":[{"options":["indicator","indicative","indicate","indications"],"answer":0},{"options":["exclude","include","preclude","conclude"],"answer":1},{"options":["contributed","contributing","contributes","contribute"],"answer":2},{"options":["who","that","what","whom"],"answer":1}],"tip":"'A ___ of economic health' needs a noun. 'It does not include' fits the criticism. 'Measures ... that reflect' uses a relative pronoun for things.","tipAr":"a + اسم (indicator). وdoes not include = لا يشمل. وthat كاسم موصول لغير العاقل (measures that reflect)."},
{"id":"rf24","title":"DNA and Heredity","text":"Deoxyribonucleic acid, known as DNA, carries the genetic instructions used in the growth and functioning of all known living organisms. Its structure, a double helix, was described in 1953 by James Watson and Francis Crick, who {1} on X-ray images produced by Rosalind Franklin. The molecule is made of four chemical bases, and the order in which they are arranged {2} the information a cell needs to build proteins. Almost every cell in the human body contains the same DNA, {3} different cells use different parts of it. Today, genetic testing can {4} inherited conditions early, giving families the chance to prepare, although it also raises difficult questions about privacy.","blanks":[{"options":["relying","relies","rely","relied"],"answer":3},{"options":["determines","determining","determine","determined"],"answer":0},{"options":["but","so","for","or"],"answer":0},{"options":["detect","detective","detection","detected"],"answer":0}],"tip":"The subject 'the order' is singular, so use 'determines'. 'But' contrasts 'the same DNA' with 'different parts'.","tipAr":"الفاعل the order مفرد فالفعل determines. وbut للتناقض بين نفس الـ DNA وأجزاء مختلفة. وبعد can فعل مصدر."},
{"id":"rf25","title":"Ice Cores","text":"Scientists drill deep into the ice sheets of Antarctica and Greenland to extract long cylinders of ice known as ice cores. Each year's snowfall forms a distinct layer, so counting the layers works rather like counting the rings of a tree. Tiny air bubbles trapped in the ice {1} samples of the ancient atmosphere, allowing researchers to measure past levels of carbon dioxide. The longest cores from Antarctica {2} climate records covering about 800,000 years. These records show that carbon dioxide concentrations today are {3} higher than at any time during that period. Because the evidence is so direct, ice cores are considered {4} the most valuable sources of information about climate history.","blanks":[{"options":["preserves","preserving","preserved","preserve"],"answer":3},{"options":["provide","providing","provides","provided"],"answer":0},{"options":["significant","signify","significantly","significance"],"answer":2},{"options":["within","between","beside","among"],"answer":3}],"tip":"Plural subjects ('bubbles', 'cores') take verbs without -s. 'Among the most valuable' is a superlative construction.","tipAr":"الفاعل جمع (bubbles / cores) فالفعل بدون s. وamong the most valuable = من أكثر المصادر قيمة. وظرف significantly يعدل higher."},
{"id":"rf26","title":"The Bauhaus","text":"The Bauhaus was a German school of art and design founded by the architect Walter Gropius in Weimar in 1919. Its teachers believed that art, craft and technology should be {1}, and that well-designed objects could improve everyday life. Students studied under painters such as Wassily Kandinsky and Paul Klee, as well as in workshops where they made furniture, textiles and metalwork. The school moved to Dessau in 1925 and later to Berlin, {2} it was closed in 1933 under pressure from the Nazi government. Many of its members then emigrated, and their ideas spread widely, {3} the style of modern buildings, chairs and typefaces around the world. Even today, simple shapes and functional design are often {4} to the school.","blanks":[{"options":["combining","combined","combination","combine"],"answer":1},{"options":["where","when","which","who"],"answer":0},{"options":["influencing","influence","influenced","influences"],"answer":0},{"options":["attended","attempted","attributed","attracted"],"answer":2}],"tip":"'Should be combined' is a passive. 'Where' refers to a place. 'Attributed to' means credited to.","tipAr":"should be + التصريف الثالث (combined). وwhere لأن Berlin مكان. وattributed to = تُنسب إلى."},
{"id":"rf27","title":"Exoplanets","text":"The first planet orbiting a Sun-like star outside our solar system was discovered in 1995, and since then astronomers have confirmed more than five thousand exoplanets. Most were found by watching for the small dip in a star's brightness that occurs when a planet passes in front of it. This method works best for planets that orbit {1} to their stars, because they cross more often. Some of the discoveries lie in the habitable zone, the region around a star where temperatures might {2} liquid water on a planet's surface. Finding water, however, does not {3} mean that life exists; researchers will need to analyse the atmospheres of these planets for chemical signs of biological activity. Newer telescopes should {4} this task considerably.","blanks":[{"options":["closeness","closely","closing","close"],"answer":3},{"options":["allow","allowing","allowed","allows"],"answer":0},{"options":["necessitate","necessity","necessarily","necessary"],"answer":2},{"options":["ease","eased","easily","easier"],"answer":0}],"tip":"'Might' + base verb. 'Does not necessarily mean' is a common academic phrase. After 'should' use a base verb.","tipAr":"بعد might فعل مصدر. وdoes not necessarily mean = لا يعني بالضرورة. وبعد should فعل مصدر (ease)."},
{"id":"rf28","title":"Microplastics","text":"Microplastics are fragments of plastic smaller than five millimetres. Some are manufactured at this size, for example the tiny beads once added to cosmetics, while others {1} when larger items such as bottles and fishing nets break down. Studies have found them in oceans, rivers, soil, and even in the air and in human blood. Because they are so small, they are very difficult to {2} from the environment once they have spread. Researchers are still investigating {3} they affect human health, and so far the evidence is limited. Many countries have already banned microbeads in cosmetics, {4} environmental groups call for stricter limits on single-use plastic.","blanks":[{"options":["forms","formed","forming","form"],"answer":3},{"options":["removal","removed","removing","remove"],"answer":3},{"options":["because","whether","whereas","unless"],"answer":1},{"options":["until","while","because","unless"],"answer":1}],"tip":"Plural subject 'others' takes 'form'. 'Investigating whether' introduces an unknown. 'Difficult to remove' needs a base verb after 'to'.","tipAr":"others جمع فالفعل form. وinvestigating whether = يبحثون إن كان. وبعد to نستخدم المصدر (remove)."}
